      "description": "University of Regina Portal | Search Jobs Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help FAQs If you need assistance, please contact Human Resources at UofR.Recruitment@uregina.ca. Search  Postings (27) Hide Search Options View all open Postings below, or enter search criteria to narrow your search. Keywords Posted Within Any time period Last Day Last Week Last Month Position Title Faculty/Department No Selection AVP (Academic) Office Centre for Continuing Education Child Trauma Research Centre (CTRC) Facilities Management Faculty of Arts Faculty of Education Faculty of Engineering and Applied Science Faculty of Graduate Studies & Research Faculty of Kinesiology and Health Studies Faculty of Media, Art, and Performance Faculty of Nursing Faculty of Science Faculty of Social Work Financial Services Hill Levene School of Business Human Resources Information Services Johnson Shoyama Graduate School La Cité Universitaire Francophone Library President's Office Provost Office Registrar's Office Student Affairs Student Affairs -Operations UR International University Advancement University Communications & Marketing University Secretariat VP Research Competition Number Category No Selection No Response Academic Executive Sessional Sessional Practica Coach Staff Student Casual Post Doctoral Fellowship (PDF) Other Employee Group No Selection CUPE 5791 CUPE 5791 - Research CUPE 2419 URFA URFA APT Out of Scope Other Post Doctoral Fellowship (PDF) Canada Research Chair (CRC) View Results (27\n    ) Competition Number Faculty/Department Category Job Close Date Employee Group Academic Skills Facilitator 20260150A/S Student Affairs Staff 09/08/2026 URFA APT Join our team at the University of Regina, where innovation, student success, and community engagement are at the core of our mission. As a leading institution committed to fostering academic excellence, we are seeking an enthusiastic and creative Academic Skills Facilitator to play a pivotal role in shaping the success and retention of our students!As an Academic Skills Facilitator with the Ac... View Details Bookmark Boiler & Building Systems Operator 20260142A/S Facilities Management Staff 09/14/2026 CUPE 5791 Are you ready to take your career to the next level in the heart of our thriving university campus? We are looking for a highly skilled and motivated individual to join our team as a Boiler & Building Systems Operator in our first class rated Heating Plant. Reporting to the Chief Engineer when assigned to the Central Heating Plant and to the Mechanical Supervisor (Preventative Maintenance) ... View Details Bookmark Lab Instructor in Visual Communication Design, Media Design (One-Year Term) 20260144A/S Faculty of Media, Art, and Performance Academic 10/15/2026 URFA The Department of Creative Technologies and Design in the Faculty of Media, Art, and Performance (MAP) at the University of Regina invites highly qualified applicants for a one-year term Lab Instructor in Visual Communication Design and/or Media Design. This is a one-year term, with the possibility of renewal, to commence January 1, 2027, or July 1, 2027.Joining an interdisciplinary team in Cre... View Details Bookmark Student Assistant - Theatre - Costume/Wardrobe - Fall 2026 20260686SS Faculty of Media, Art, and Performance Student 09/07/2026 CUPE 2419 Various work related to projects, duties, and maintenance within the designated areas of the Costume Shop. View Details Bookmark Executive Assistant to the Associate Vice-President, Finance 20260151A/S Financial Services Staff 09/14/2026 Out of Scope Are you a master of organization with a knack for anticipating needs before they arise? We’re looking for a proactive, detail-driven Executive Assistant to support our leadership team and keep operations running seamlessly behind the scenes.The Executive Assistant provides senior-level administrative, operational, and strategic support to the Associate Vice-President, Finance. As the operationa... View Details Bookmark Teaching Assistant - MAP 101 Intro to Pop Culture- Fall 2026 20260693SS Faculty of Media, Art, and Performance Student 09/07/2026 CUPE 2419 This Teaching Assistant offers support for delivering an undergraduate in-person course by assisting with marking assignments and other related duties as assigned.MAP 101 is a 6-week course and student assignments will be ongoing and consistent during this time. Grading and deadlines will come up quickly.There is an in-person final exam for this course. View Details Bookmark Teaching Assistant - 202630- CRIM 276-001-Professional Ethics 20260625SS Faculty of Arts Student 09/06/2026 CUPE 2419 Assist instructor as required with marking and provide electronic feedback to students on assignments. Assist with student email/discussion board inquiries and postings. Must be available to attend regular meetings with the instructor if required, and be available to attend some classes in the course to which they are assigned if required by the instructor. View Details Bookmark Teaching Assistant -202630-CRIM 230-991- Intro to Canadian Law (CCE) 20260624SS Faculty of Arts Student 09/06/2026 CUPE 2419 Assist instructor as required with marking and provide electronic feedback to students on assignments. Assist with student email/discussion board inquiries and postings. Must be available to attend regular meetings with the instructor if required, and be available to attend some classes in the course to which they are assigned if required by the instructor. View Details Bookmark Teaching Assistant - 202630- CRIM 201-991- Criminal Justice System (CCE) 20260623SS Faculty of Arts Student 09/06/2026 CUPE 2419 Assist instructor as required with marking and provide electronic feedback to students on assignments. Assist with student email/discussion board inquiries and postings. Must be available to attend regular meetings with the instructor if required, and be available to attend some classes in the course to which they are assigned if required by the instructor. View Details Bookmark Teaching Assistant - 202630- CRIM 101-0A1 Introduction to Criminology (CCE) 20260628SS Faculty of Arts Student 09/06/2026 CUPE 2419 Assist instructor as required with marking and provide electronic feedback to students on assignments. Assist with student email/discussion board inquiries and postings. Must be available to attend regular meetings with the instructor if required, and be available to attend some classes in the course to which they are assigned if required by the instructor. View Details Bookmark Teaching Assistant (2) - 202630-CRIM 101-002 - Introduction to Criminology 20260630SS Faculty of Arts Student 09/06/2026 CUPE 2419 Assist instructor as required with marking and provide electronic feedback to students on assignments. Assist with student email/discussion board inquiries and postings. Must be available to attend regular meetings with the instructor if required, and be available to attend some classes in the course to which they are assigned if required by the instructor. View Details Bookmark Teaching Assistant 2 - 202630-CRIM 101-001 Introduction to Criminology 20260629SS Faculty of Arts Student 09/06/2026 CUPE 2419 Assist instructor as required with marking and provide electronic feedback to students on assignments. Assist with student email/discussion board inquiries and postings. Must be available to attend regular meetings with the instructor if required, and be available to attend some classes in the course to which they are assigned if required by the instructor. View Details Bookmark Student Teaching Assistant for for EC&I 871 Indigenous Spirituality in Ed 20260689SS Faculty of Education Student 09/03/2026 CUPE 2419 The successful applicant will provide support with course editing and marking.Duties may include:Evaluating course assignments using established rubricsOther duties that may be assigned by the instructor from time to time View Details Bookmark Student Teaching Assistant for ECS 303-030: Curriculum and Pedagogy 20260673SS Faculty of Education Student 09/03/2026 CUPE 2419 The successful applicant will provide support for the delivery of undergraduate courses by assisting with providing feedback on assignments and projects.Duties may include:Evaluating course assignments using established rubricsProviding feedback and suggestions on assignmentsOther duties that may be assigned by the instructor from time to time View Details Bookmark Student Research Assistant - Participant Pool Coordinator 20260684SS Faculty of Arts Student 09/06/2026 CUPE 2419 The Participant Pool Coordinator is responsible for all operations relating to the Psychology Participant Pool’s functions, maintenance, and technical support within SONA Systems, the participant pool software. These tasks will involve participant pool set-up, creating and / or approving research studies, assisting with questions, study maintenance & technical support, generating credit rep... View Details Bookmark Director, Financial Operations 20260148A/S Financial Services Staff 09/04/2026 Out of Scope Are you a strategic and collaborative financial leader, ready to guide high-performing teams while ensuring strong financial controls and accurate payment, reporting, and risk management practices? Join us as our new Director, Financial Operations!The Director, Financial Operations provides senior leadership over institutional financial operations, reporting, and decision support within a compl... View Details Bookmark Graduate Student Research Assistant (Multiple) 20260670SS Johnson Shoyama Graduate School Student 09/15/2026 CUPE 2419 This position is open to currently registered graduate students at the University of Regina. The student(s) will assist with a project exploring risk perceptions and public attitudes towards nuclear science, nuclear energy (and its lifecycle), climate change, and social learning.Duties include:Research activities including (but not limited to) literature reviews, including legal and regulatory ... View Details Bookmark Teaching Assistants for Geography & Environmental Studies - Fall 2026 20260657SS Faculty of Arts Student 09/07/2026 CUPE 2419 Multiple TA positions are available.Duties will normally consist of: assisting with the instructional program of undergraduate courses, assisting with research on curriculum development for a course, and/or marking assignments or tests, and tutoring; and/or leading lab sections (where applicable), with associated marking, preparation and assignments. Assisting in the Map Library. View Details Bookmark Sessional Supervisor for Pre-Internship (le Bac) - Fall 2026 /Responsable de stage pour la pré-stage (niveau bac) - Automne 2026 20260655SS Faculty of Education Sessional 09/03/2026 URFA Successful candidates will be assigned to supervise pre-intern student teachers for the Bac Program in Regina and/or throughout the province. They will act as liaison persons for the faculty and offer resources, guidance and support for the cooperating teacher and pre-interns. Sessional supervisors are expected to be available to visit and provide support/guidance as needed by the pre-interns a... View Details Bookmark Tenure-Track Assistant Professor: Language and Literacy/Early Childhood Education 20260133A/S Faculty of Education Academic 09/30/2026 URFA The Faculty of Education at the University of Regina invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Language and Literacy/Early Childhood Education, with an anticipated start date of January 1, 2027, or as negotiated with the successful candidate. This hybrid position has a primary focus on early and emergent literacy with a connection to early childhood educ... View Details Bookmark Clinical Nursing Practica Coach - Regina 20260580SS Faculty of Nursing Sessional Practica Coach URFA The Faculty of Nursing invites applications for clinical nursing practica coaches. Registered Nurses or Registered Psychiatric Nurses with recent practice education experience across multiple care areas are encouraged to apply. The position encompasses the instruction, supervision, mentorship, and evaluation of nursing students in various practice education, community, and lab/seminar settings ... View Details Bookmark Clinical Nursing Practica Coach - Saskatoon 20260579SS Faculty of Nursing Sessional Practica Coach URFA The Faculty of Nursing invites applications for clinical nursing practica coaches. Registered Nurses or Registered Psychiatric Nurses with recent clinical experience across multiple care areas are encouraged to apply. The position encompasses the instruction, supervision, mentorship, and evaluation of nursing students in various practice education, community, and lab/seminar settings throughout... View Details Bookmark Clinical Nursing Practica Coach - North Battleford 20260578SS Faculty of Nursing Sessional Practica Coach URFA Position Summary:The Faculty of Nursing invites applications for clinical nursing practica coaches. Registered Nurses or Registered Psychiatric Nurses with recent clinical experience across multiple care areas are encouraged to apply.The position encompasses the instruction, supervision, mentorship, and evaluation of nursing students in various clinical, community, and lab/seminar settings thro... View Details Bookmark Casual Administrative Positions (University of Regina students) 20260026SS Human Resources Student 12/31/2026 CUPE 5791 The University of Regina is seeking University of Regina students interested in casual and short-term clerical positions. A pool of candidates is needed immediately to meet the needs of various departments or units. The applicants would be expected to carry out a variety of office duties.The purpose of this posting is for applicants that would be able to fill casual and short term positions as ... View Details Bookmark Casual Administrative Positions (Non-Student) 20260008A/S Human Resources Staff 12/31/2026 CUPE 5791 The University of Regina is seeking individuals interested in casual and short-term clerical positions. A pool of candidates is needed to meet the needs of various departments and units on campus. The applicants would be expected to carry out a variety of office duties.The purpose of this posting is to build a pool of candidates for casual and short term positions. This pool will be refreshed o... View Details Bookmark Assistant Professor, Developmental Psychology 20250495A/S Faculty of Arts Academic URFA The Department of Psychology at the University of Regina is seeking applications for a full-time, tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor, with expertise in developmental psychology. The anticipated date of commencement is July 1, 2025, depending on the availability of the successful candidate.Duties of the successful candidate will include teaching at the undergraduate and gra... View Details Bookmark Open-Rank Faculty Professor Position in Clinical Psychology 20240170A/S Faculty of Arts Academic URFA The University of Regina is a vibrant and growing campus in a province with a booming economy. The Department of Psychology comprises a large undergraduate and honours program in addition to experimental and clinical graduate programs and has received numerous accolades for its research output and impact. Most recently, a paper published in Canadian Psychology (https://dx.doi.org/10.1037/cap000... View Details Bookmark If you need assistance, please contact Human Resources at UofR.Recruitment@uregina.ca . To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
