    "https://urcareers.uregina.ca/postings/all_jobs.atom": {
      "title": "",
      "description": "<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<feed xml:lang=\"en-US\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom\" xmlns:pa=\"urcareers.uregina.ca\">\n  <id>tag:urcareers.uregina.ca,2005:/postings/all_jobs</id>\n  <link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"text/html\" href=\"https://urcareers.uregina.ca\"/>\n  <link rel=\"self\" type=\"application/atom+xml\" href=\"https://urcareers.uregina.ca/postings/all_jobs.atom\"/>\n  <title>University of Regina: All Jobs</title>\n  <updated>2024-11-25T11:24:21-06:00</updated>\n  <entry>\n    <id>https://urcareers.uregina.ca/postings/17692</id>\n    <published>2024-11-25T11:24:21-06:00</published>\n    <updated>2024-11-25T11:24:21-06:00</updated>\n    <link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"text/html\" href=\"https://urcareers.uregina.ca/postings/17692\"/>\n    <title>Open-Rank Faculty Professor Position in Clinical Psychology</title>\n    <content>&lt;div&gt;The University of Regina is a vibrant and growing campus in a province with a booming economy. The Department of Psychology comprises a large undergraduate and honours program in addition to experimental and clinical graduate programs and has received numerous accolades for its research output and impact. Most recently, a paper published in Canadian Psychology (&lt;a href=\"https://dx.doi.org/10.1037/cap0000378\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;https://dx.doi.org/10.1037/cap0000378&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;) identified 3 department faculty as being amongst the top 15% most productive clinical psychologists in Canada.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;As part of an ongoing expansion of the Clinical Psychology Graduate Program, the Department of Psychology at the University of Regina is seeking applications for an open rank position in Clinical Psychology. Area of clinical research specialization is open, and rank of the position will be commensurate with experience. Date of commencement is negotiable depending on the availability of the successful candidate, but we wish to fill this position as soon as possible.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Duties of the successful candidate will include teaching at the undergraduate and graduate level, honours and graduate thesis supervision, supervision of clinical practicums, and participation in departmental activities. The successful candidate is expected to have an independent and active program of research in clinical psychology that would be eligible for Tri-Council and/or Canada Foundation for Innovation funding.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;The University of Regina's Strategic Plan 2020-2025 (kahkiyaw kiwâhkômâkaninawak – All Our Relations) emphasizes Well-being and Belonging as a strategic priority, which includes prioritizing and supporting research in mental health. The Clinical Psychology Graduate Program at the University of Regina is committed to the &lt;em&gt;scientist-practitioner&lt;/em&gt; model and is &lt;strong&gt;accredited by the Canadian Psychological Association&lt;/strong&gt;. The Clinical Psychology Graduate Program has an on-site state-of-the-art Psychology Training Clinic. The Department maintains good relations with a number of health care, research, and other educational facilities both within Regina and throughout the province.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Review of applications will continue until the position is filled.&lt;/div&gt;</content>\n    <author>\n      <name>Arts-Psychology</name>\n    </author>\n  </entry>\n  <entry>\n    <id>https://urcareers.uregina.ca/postings/21148</id>\n    <published>2026-01-09T09:45:58-06:00</published>\n    <updated>2026-01-09T09:45:58-06:00</updated>\n    <link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"text/html\" href=\"https://urcareers.uregina.ca/postings/21148\"/>\n    <title>Casual Administrative Positions (Non-Student)</title>\n    <content>&lt;div&gt;The University of Regina is seeking individuals interested in casual and short-term clerical positions. A pool of candidates is needed to meet the needs of various departments and units on campus. The applicants would be expected to carry out a variety of office duties.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The purpose of this posting is to build a pool of candidates for casual and short term positions. This pool will be refreshed on an annual basis.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</content>\n    <author>\n      <name>Human Resources - Org Dev &amp; People Programs</name>\n    </author>\n  </entry>\n  <entry>\n    <id>https://urcareers.uregina.ca/postings/22926</id>\n    <published>2026-08-20T16:25:49-06:00</published>\n    <updated>2026-08-20T16:25:50-06:00</updated>\n    <link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"text/html\" href=\"https://urcareers.uregina.ca/postings/22926\"/>\n    <title>Director, Financial Operations</title>\n    <content>&lt;div&gt;Are you a strategic and collaborative financial leader, ready to guide high-performing teams while ensuring strong financial controls and accurate payment, reporting, and risk management practices?&lt;strong&gt; Join us as our new Director, Financial Operations!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Director, Financial Operations provides senior leadership over institutional financial operations, reporting, and decision support within a complex post-secondary environment, ensuring strong financial stewardship, internal controls, and compliance with applicable accounting standards, regulatory requirements, and governance frameworks.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;The role is responsible for the effective oversight of core financial operations, including budget administration, operating fund management, transactional financial processes, and specialized financial activities such as research finance, trust, and endowment reporting. This includes ensuring accuracy, integrity, and consistency of financial information used for both internal management and external compliance purposes.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;In addition, the Director leads the development and continuous improvement of financial reporting, analytics, and decision support capabilities across the institution. This includes advancing the use of financial systems, data tools, and reporting platforms to improve access to timely, reliable, and actionable financial information for senior leadership and decentralized units.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;A key aspect of the role is leading the modernization of financial operations through process improvement, automation, and the implementation of scalable, technology-enabled solutions. The Director is accountable for strengthening operational efficiency, enhancing financial controls, and supporting the transition toward a more integrated, data-driven environment that enables informed decision-making and institutional accountability.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial Stewardship and Budget Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Direct the management and execution of a $400M/Yr operating budget and resource allocation framework, ensuring disciplined financial stewardship and long-term sustainability.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Ensure effective oversight of core financial operations, including budgeting processes, adjustments, budget surplus management, and other transactional activities, while advancing automation and process improvement.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Provide leadership and change management to support successful adoption of new tools, systems, and processes across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Financial Reporting and Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Provide best-in-class financial analysis and reporting practices, aligned with accounting standards, legislative and regulatory requirements, and internal governance frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Ensure effective management of specialized financial operations, including trust and endowment administration and financial compliance reporting.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial Systems and Reporting Technology&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Lead adoption and use of technology within Financial Services, including financial systems, reporting platforms, and data tools, to enhance efficiency and reporting capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Oversee design and implementation of self-service reporting tools and dashboards, grounded in strong accounting knowledge to ensure accuracy, relevance, and actionable insight.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Lead initiatives to improve data availability, consistency, and usability, supporting a “single source of truth” for institutional financial information.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process Improvements and Transformation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Drive process improvement and automation initiatives to reduce manual effort, improve accuracy and response times and strengthen financial controls across core finance functions.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Advance the transition from manual, transactional processes to automated, scalable workflows while maintaining strong governance, controls, and compliance.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Translate business and operational needs into technology-enabled solutions that improve operations, reporting, and decision support.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial Advisory and Stakeholder Engagement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Lead the provision of financial advisory services to senior leadership and faculties, with clear accountability for financial analysis, recommendations, and decision support.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Lead stakeholder engagement and communication across a large, complex, decentralized organization, building trusted relationships and translating complex financial data into clear, actionable insights and recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Monitor financial performance, identify variances, and provide actionable recommendations to unit leadership to support effective financial management.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People Leadership and Performance Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Lead a multidisciplinary team across budget operations, research finance, accounts payable, and banking within a unionized environment.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Build team capability in analytics, advisory services, and reporting to support decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of rapid response, accountability, service excellence, and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Support and develop staff capabilities while leading change initiatives to implement new tools, processes, and ways of working.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Plus More: &lt;/strong&gt;Be ready to take on additional related tasks as assigned – your role is dynamic and essential to our success!&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;At the University of Regina, we’re more than just a campus – we’re a community!&lt;br&gt;Join our team and enjoy:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Meaningful Impact: &lt;/strong&gt;Your work directly contributes to creating a better environment for students, faculty, and staff.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Professional Growth: &lt;/strong&gt;We support your development, offering opportunities for advancement and learning.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work-Life Balance:&lt;/strong&gt; We value your well-being and know your personal life is most important!&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamic and Inclusive Workplace: &lt;/strong&gt;We value diversity and inclusivity. You’ll be part of a team that celebrates different perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences, making every day an opportunity for personal growth.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovation Culture: &lt;/strong&gt;We encourage fresh ideas and innovative thinking.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Competitive Compensation:&lt;/strong&gt; We offer competitive compensation package and benefits to reward your talent. A few of the these benefits include Health/Dental/Vision Benefits, flexible spending account, Defined Contribution Pension Plan, and much more!&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;If you are ready to join a dynamic team and make a difference, we invite you to apply today!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</content>\n    <author>\n      <name>Financial Services - Executive Reporting Services</name>\n    </author>\n  </entry>\n  <entry>\n    <id>https://urcareers.uregina.ca/postings/22967</id>\n    <published>2026-09-01T12:01:24-06:00</published>\n    <updated>2026-09-01T12:01:24-06:00</updated>\n    <link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"text/html\" href=\"https://urcareers.uregina.ca/postings/22967\"/>\n    <title>Lab Instructor in Visual Communication Design, Media Design (One-Year Term)</title>\n    <content>&lt;div&gt;The Department of Creative Technologies and Design in the Faculty of Media, Art, and Performance (MAP) at the University of Regina invites highly qualified applicants for a one-year term Lab Instructor in Visual Communication Design and/or Media Design. This is a one-year term, with the possibility of renewal, to commence January 1, 2027, or July 1, 2027.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Joining an interdisciplinary team in Creative Technologies and Design, Fine Arts, Media, Computer Science, and Engineering, the successful candidate will bring technical expertise and critical thinking in the areas of Visual Communication Design and/or Media Design to build upon the well-established strengths of the Department of Creative Technologies and Design as we continue to expand our programs.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Teaching will include studio, lab-based, and lecture formats, as well as online and mixed modalities at the undergraduate level in Creative Technologies and Design. Previous studio/lab-based teaching experience at the University level in one or more of the areas of Visual Communication Design and Media Design, including Graphic Design, Web Design, Data Visualization, Advertising and Marketing Design, UI and UX Design, or Digital Interaction Design is required.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;The successful candidate will be expected to teach 7 undergraduate courses and contribute to service in the Department of Creative Technologies and Design and MAP.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;We acknowledge that within higher education in Canada, traditional or conventional academic and artistic pathways can reinforce biases in the filling of faculty and instructor positions. We encourage applications from those who may not fit all the qualifications and that challenge our ideas of teaching and artistic practice. We are particularly interested in colleagues who bring experience in facilitating equity, diversity and inclusion practices within their teaching, which may include contexts outside of the academic domain, including artistic praxis and community-based work.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Creative Technologies and Design seeks to attract candidates who identify with under-represented groups, and who are able to articulate a teaching philosophy that aligns with our values and complements and builds upon the established socially-engaged practices for which the Department is known. We seek a candidate whose expertise will enhance the University of Regina’s growing reputation as an important centre for a variety of teaching and research endeavours, including Indigenous art practices, disability/atypical creative practices, community wellness, social justice, community engaged creative practices, media arts, curation, exhibition and/or performance practices.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;The University of Regina is located in the heart of a vibrant, and increasingly diverse, mid-sized city in the center of the beautiful Canadian prairies on Treaty 4 Territory. The University has a student population of 16,000+ and is home to 10 faculties, including a multitude of academic departments and program areas. These units have established national and international reputations for excellence and innovative programs leading to bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degrees. The University has three federated colleges: First Nations University of Canada, Campion College, and Luther College. Our colleges bring further excellence and diversity to the educational experiences we offer.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;With a faculty complement of 35 full-time professors, including some of the most celebrated contemporary artists in the country, MAP enjoys a long-standing reputation as one of Western Canada’s foremost environments for scholarship and artistic research at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Emphasizing the importance of studio production and theory, we offer BA, BFA, BMus, MMus, MA, MFA, and an Interdisciplinary Studies PhD in Media and Artistic Practices.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;MAP works with other units, such as First Nations University of Canada, Women and Gender Studies, Social Work, Computer Science, Engineering, Business, Arts, Education, Kinesiology, and the Humanities Research Institute. MAP is home to the Centre for Socially Engaged Theatre (CSET), IMP Lab (Interactive Media and Performance), the VOICE Lab (Vocally Oriented Investigations in Creative Expression), RISC (Regina Improvisation Studies Centre). We have strong collaborative relationships with arts institutions, such as the MacKenzie Art Gallery, Regina Symphony Orchestra, Sâkêwêwak Artist Collective, Dunlop Art Gallery, Art Gallery of Regina, Regina Public Library, Neutral Ground, New Dance Horizons, Saskatchewan Film Pool, and Common Weal, among others. MAP has numerous international partnership universities, with many innovative mobility initiatives for both faculty and students in Mexico City and the UK, among other locations. MAP is now home to a new Canada Research Chair in Socially Engaged Theatre (Tier II) and the SaskPower Chair in Cultural Heritage.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;The University of Regina is strongly committed to employment equity within its communities and to recruiting a diverse faculty and staff.&lt;/div&gt;</content>\n    <author>\n      <name>Media, Art, and Performance-Other</name>\n    </author>\n  </entry>\n  <entry>\n    <id>https://urcareers.uregina.ca/postings/22976</id>\n    <published>2026-09-02T18:56:37-06:00</published>\n    <updated>2026-09-02T18:56:37-06:00</updated>\n    <link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"text/html\" href=\"https://urcareers.uregina.ca/postings/22976\"/>\n    <title>Academic Skills Facilitator</title>\n    <content>&lt;div&gt;Join our team at the University of Regina, where innovation, student success, and community engagement are at the core of our mission. As a leading institution committed to fostering academic excellence, we are seeking an enthusiastic and creative &lt;strong&gt;Academic Skills Facilitator&lt;/strong&gt; to play a pivotal role in shaping the success and retention of our students!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;As an Academic Skills Facilitator with the Academic Transition Programs, you will be a key contributor to our University's strategic enrollment management initiative. Your primary focus will be on developing, overseeing, and delivering programs tailored to the success and retention of new and continuing undergraduate students experiencing academic difficulties or personal challenges.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You'll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Implement and Deliver:&lt;/strong&gt; Facilitate the Academic Recovery Program and Arts Transition Program for academically at-risk students.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Individual and Group Advising:&lt;/strong&gt; Conduct personalized sessions, identifying reasons for academic challenges, and devising strategies to enhance students' skills and motivation.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Progress Monitoring:&lt;/strong&gt; Track and monitor students' progress in the programs, ensuring timely intervention and support.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Facilitation:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead weekly sessions and other program components, fostering an engaging and supportive learning environment.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and implement a comprehensive communication strategy to promote the programs and engage students effectively.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Train, and supervise student teaching assistants, ensuring a cohesive and efficient team.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Records Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Oversee records management, appointment scheduling, database updates, and outreach to potential students.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Establish and maintain collaborative relationships with University staff, contributing to a unified and student-centric approach.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Program Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Collaborate on developing and delivering new programming, tailoring solutions to specific student needs.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design and Delivery:&lt;/strong&gt; Design course material and presentations, and contribute to program promotion, curriculum review, and evaluation.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Plus More: &lt;/strong&gt;Be ready to take on additional related tasks as assigned – your role is dynamic and essential to our success!&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;At the University of Regina, we are more than just a campus – we are a community! Join our team and enjoy:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Meaningful Impact: &lt;/strong&gt;Your work directly contributes to creating a better environment for students, faculty, and staff.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Professional Growth: &lt;/strong&gt;We support your development, offering opportunities for advancement and learning.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work-Life Balance:&lt;/strong&gt; We value your well-being and know your personal life is most important!&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamic and Inclusive Workplace: &lt;/strong&gt;We value diversity and inclusivity. You’ll be part of a team that celebrates different perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences, making every day an opportunity for personal growth.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovation Culture: &lt;/strong&gt;We encourage fresh ideas and innovative thinking.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Competitive Compensation: &lt;/strong&gt;We offer competitive compensation package and benefits to reward your talent. A few of the these benefits include Health/Dental/Vision Benefits, flexible spending account, Defined Contribution Pension Plan, and much more!&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;If you are an energetic and innovative individual passionate about developing and implementing retention programming targeted to undergraduate students experiencing academic difficulties or personal challenges, we invite you to apply today!&lt;/div&gt;</content>\n    <author>\n      <name>SA - Student Success Centre</name>\n    </author>\n  </entry>\n  <entry>\n    <id>https://urcareers.uregina.ca/postings/18787</id>\n    <published>2025-04-04T15:59:11-06:00</published>\n    <updated>2025-04-04T15:59:12-06:00</updated>\n    <link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"text/html\" href=\"https://urcareers.uregina.ca/postings/18787\"/>\n    <title>Assistant Professor, Developmental Psychology</title>\n    <content>&lt;div&gt;The Department of Psychology at the University of Regina is seeking applications for a full-time, tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor, with expertise in developmental psychology. The anticipated date of commencement is July 1, 2025, depending on the availability of the successful candidate.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Duties of the successful candidate will include teaching at the undergraduate and graduate level, honours and graduate thesis supervision, participation in departmental activities, and administrative service within the department. The successful candidate is expected to develop an independent program of research in developmental psychology that would be eligible for Tri-Council and/or Canada Foundation for Innovation funding.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;The University of Regina's Strategic Plan 2020-2025 (kahkiyaw kiwâhkômâkaninawak – All Our Relations) emphasizes Well-being and Belonging as a strategic priority, which includes prioritizing and supporting research in mental health. The Department of Psychology has been recognized as &lt;a href=\"https://www.timeshighereducation.com/world-university-rankings/2025/subject-ranking/psychology#!/length/25/sort_by/scores_citations/sort_order/asc/cols/scores\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;#1 in Canada and #2 in the world&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; in research quality, and is frequently &lt;a href=\"https://www.timeshighereducation.com/world-university-rankings/2022/subject-ranking/psychology#!/length/25/locations/CAN/sort_by/rank/sort_order/asc/cols/stats\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ranked among the top psychology departments in Canada&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. The Department offers two graduate programs, including the Experimental and Applied Psychology Graduate Program and the Clinical Psychology Graduate Program. The latter is accredited by the Canadian Psychological Association and has an on-site state-of-the-art Psychology Training Clinic. The Department maintains good relations with a number of health care, policing, research, and other educational facilities both within Regina and throughout the province.&lt;/div&gt;</content>\n    <author>\n      <name>Arts-Psychology</name>\n    </author>\n  </entry>\n  <entry>\n    <id>https://urcareers.uregina.ca/postings/22779</id>\n    <published>2026-08-04T13:12:00-06:00</published>\n    <updated>2026-08-04T13:12:01-06:00</updated>\n    <link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"text/html\" href=\"https://urcareers.uregina.ca/postings/22779\"/>\n    <title>Tenure-Track Assistant Professor: Language and Literacy/Early Childhood Education</title>\n    <content>&lt;div&gt;The Faculty of Education at the University of Regina invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track&lt;strong&gt; Assistant Professor position in Language and Literacy/Early Childhood Education&lt;/strong&gt;, with an anticipated start date of&lt;strong&gt; January 1, 2027, or as negotiated with the successful candidate.&lt;/strong&gt; This hybrid position has a primary focus on early and emergent literacy with a connection to early childhood education.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;The University of Regina is located on Treaty 4 territory, with a presence in Treaty 6. These lands are home to the nêhiyawak, Anihšināpēk, Dakota, Lakota, and Nakoda peoples, and the homeland of the Métis/Michif Nation. With a population of over 270,000, Regina offers a rich blend of cultural, recreational, and entertainment opportunities—providing big-city amenities with a small-town feel.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;The Faculty of Education offers a variety of programs at both the undergraduate and graduate levels and engages in local, national, and international programs and projects in French and English. The Faculty of Education is committed to enacting social and ecological justice, indigenization, sustainability, cultural and linguistic diversity, life-long learning, service, outreach, and the collaborative processes that flourish in a community of caring and mutual respect. Our mission embodies commitments to community engagement, innovative research, and student success, as articulated in the University of Regina’s Strategic Plan &lt;em&gt;Together, We Serve: Community, Discovery, Impact.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Duties&lt;/strong&gt;: The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Language and Literacy, as well as selected Early Childhood Education courses. Expertise in reading pedagogies for young readers and emergent literacy development is required. The candidate will be expected to maintain an active program of scholarly research, independently and/or collaboratively, and to supervise and mentor graduate students. In addition, the successful candidate will contribute to collegial governance through service on faculty and university committees, as well as engagement with professional and broader communities.&lt;/div&gt;</content>\n    <author>\n      <name>Education-Dean's Office</name>\n    </author>\n  </entry>\n  <entry>\n    <id>https://urcareers.uregina.ca/postings/22965</id>\n    <published>2026-09-01T10:17:39-06:00</published>\n    <updated>2026-09-01T10:17:39-06:00</updated>\n    <link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"text/html\" href=\"https://urcareers.uregina.ca/postings/22965\"/>\n    <title>Executive Assistant to the Associate Vice-President, Finance</title>\n    <content>&lt;div&gt;Are you a master of organization with a knack for anticipating needs before they arise? We’re looking for a proactive, detail-driven Executive Assistant to support our leadership team and keep operations running seamlessly behind the scenes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Executive Assistant provides senior-level administrative, operational, and strategic support to the Associate Vice-President, Finance. As the operational hub of the Office of the Associate Vice-President, Finance, the position ensures the seamless coordination of executive priorities, budget administration, governance activities, information management, and stakeholder engagement. The role serves as a trusted executive partner, enabling the Associate Vice-President to remain focused on strategic objectives, critical decisions, institutional priorities, and the successful administration of the University's financial operations.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;The role requires a highly adaptable and resilient professional who thrives in a dynamic environment characterized by evolving demands. The incumbent needs to exercise exceptional judgment, initiative, and discretion to anticipate priorities, manage competing commitments, and proactively address emerging issues while maintaining strong stakeholder relationships, confidentiality, and service excellence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Executive Office Leadership and Administration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Provide senior-level administrative and operational support to the Associate Vice-President, Finance.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Manage a highly complex and dynamic calendar, coordinating meetings, priorities, travel arrangements, and executive commitments.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Serve as a strategic partner to the Associate Vice-President by monitoring priorities, tracking key deliverables and commitments, coordinating follow-up activities, and ensuring critical deadlines, decisions, and institutional obligations are effectively managed.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and support executive, budget, governance, and committee meetings, including scheduling, agenda development, preparation of materials, recording of minutes, and follow-up on action items.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Prepare, edit, and quality-assure executive correspondence, reports, briefing materials, presentations, governance documents, Board materials, and public-facing communications, ensuring accuracy, consistency, clarity, and professionalism.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Maintain the highest standards of confidentiality, professionalism, and discretion when handling sensitive financial and organizational information.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Budget Process Leadership and Coordination&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Working in partnership with the Associate Vice-President, Finance, lead the coordination and administration of the University's annual operating budget process.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Administer the institution's annual budget schedule, ensuring budget materials are prepared and distributed, information is collected and compiled, and milestones, deadlines, and approval requirements are met.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Coordinate budget planning and review meetings with academic and administrative units and Financial Services staff.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Prepare and distribute budget templates, schedules, instructions, and supporting materials.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Collect, consolidate, organize, and track budget submissions and related documentation from faculties, departments, and administrative units.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Monitor progress throughout the budget cycle and follow up with stakeholders to ensure timelines, deliverables, and reporting requirements are achieved.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Compile and summarize budget information and supporting documentation for presentations, reports, and materials prepared for senior leadership, governance committees, and the Board of Governors.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Information Management and Executive Communications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary administrator for Finance SharePoint sites and information repositories.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Manage document libraries, records, workflows, templates, reports, and executive files, ensuring information is organized, accessible, current, and compliant with records management requirements.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Support the continuous improvement of information management practices, administrative processes, and digital workflows.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Provide advanced editorial and quality assurance support for presentations, financial reports, Board materials, executive correspondence, and public-facing documents, ensuring accuracy, consistency, clarity, and the highest standards of professionalism.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Relations and Portfolio Coordination&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Act as a key liaison between Financial Services, academic and administrative units, senior leaders, government representatives, and external stakeholders to support effective communication, collaboration, and issue resolution.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Support the coordination of strategic and operational initiatives within the Finance portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Foster strong working relationships and provide exceptional service in support of University priorities.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Plus More: &lt;/strong&gt;Be ready to take on additional related tasks as assigned – your role is dynamic and essential to our success!&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;At the University of Regina, we’re more than just a campus – we’re a community!&lt;br&gt;Join our team and enjoy:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Meaningful Impact: &lt;/strong&gt;Your work directly contributes to creating a better environment for students, faculty, and staff.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Professional Growth: &lt;/strong&gt;We support your development, offering opportunities for advancement and learning.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work-Life Balance:&lt;/strong&gt; We value your well-being and know your personal life is most important!&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamic and Inclusive Workplace: &lt;/strong&gt;We value diversity and inclusivity. You’ll be part of a team that celebrates different perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences, making every day an opportunity for personal growth.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovation Culture: &lt;/strong&gt;We encourage fresh ideas and innovative thinking.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Competitive Compensation:&lt;/strong&gt; We offer competitive compensation package and benefits to reward your talent. A few of the these benefits include Health/Dental/Vision Benefits, flexible spending account, Defined Contribution Pension Plan, and much more!&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;If you’re ready to join a dynamic team, we invite you to apply today!&lt;/div&gt;</content>\n    <author>\n      <name>Financial Services-AVP Finance</name>\n    </author>\n  </entry>\n  <entry>\n    <id>https://urcareers.uregina.ca/postings/22968</id>\n    <published>2026-09-01T14:31:13-06:00</published>\n    <updated>2026-09-01T14:31:14-06:00</updated>\n    <link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"text/html\" href=\"https://urcareers.uregina.ca/postings/22968\"/>\n    <title>Boiler &amp; Building Systems Operator</title>\n    <content>&lt;div&gt;Are you ready to take your career to the next level in the heart of our thriving university campus? We are looking for a highly skilled and motivated individual to join our team as a &lt;strong&gt;Boiler &amp;amp; Building Systems Operator &lt;/strong&gt;in our first class rated Heating Plant. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Reporting to the Chief Engineer when assigned to the Central Heating Plant and to the Mechanical Supervisor (Preventative Maintenance) when assigned to the Utilities Maintenance Crew, this position offers an exciting opportunity to play a pivotal role in the operation and maintenance of our heating plant and auxiliary systems. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The incumbent will be responsible for carrying out assigned operating and maintenance duties within the University of Regina's heating plant and/or Utilities Maintenance Crew. When assigned to the heating plant, the position is under the supervision of the Shift Engineer, in accordance with the Boiler and Pressure Vessel Act and Regulations. The incumbent is also responsible for assisting in the operation and maintenance of the heating plant's high pressure steam boilers, refrigeration equipment, and all associated auxiliary equipment and systems. When conditions and work load permit, this position may also be assigned to the Utilities Maintenance Crew under the supervision of the Mechanical Supervisor (Preventative Maintenance).&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;br&gt;Heating Plant:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Assist the Shift Engineer with the operations and maintenance of the plant equipment and systems, including but not limited to locking out and tagging out of plant equipment, identifying breakdowns and repairs as appropriate, informing operating condition of the HP, etc.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Monitor, check and log operating systems of boilers, chillers and auxiliary equipment.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Make alterations to regulate the flow of feed water, condensate and make-up water within the systems.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Start and stop boilers, chillers, and auxiliary equipment.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Clean boilers, sumps, tanks, chillers including brushing condensers and evaporator tubes, etc.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Repack valves and pumps.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Change filters and clean strainers on systems in the plant.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Check, tighten and change belts on plant equipment.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Check oil levels and change oil in plant equipment.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Grease and lubricate plant equipment.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Complete and record assigned preventative maintenance checks.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Assist internal maintenance personnel and external contractor working in the heating plant.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Sample, test and record boiler, chilled and condenser waters. Make necessary changes to chemical feed rates to maintain desired levels.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Regenerate softener and clean RO membranes.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Monitor fire alarm panels and plant phones.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Perform weekly checks of all back-up equipment and alarms.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Record chemical inventories.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Move chemical barrels from loading dock to basement storage areas.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Provide guidance to student operator personnel.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Other related duties as assigned.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Utilities Maintenance Crew:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Inspect all mechanical equipment and systems to mitigate damage and down time.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Perform daily, weekly, monthly and annual preventative maintenance on equipment to ensure life cycle.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Perform monthly chemical tests to maintain integrity of distribution lines and infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Record meter readings for utility charges and identifying possible issues of abnormal usage.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Maintain housekeeping in all restricted areas to maintain a high level of safe working conditions for everyone.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Respond to emergency situations in order to resolve issues as quickly as possible.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Maintain positive relations with all building contacts and occupants by communicating in advance.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Make daily decisions regarding safe work strategies in private and public areas.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Manage stock material orders, pick up and deliver supplies and record anomalies for correction.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Asset management regarding equipment and updating information&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Monthly maintenance as per service schedules including greasing bearings, bolt tensioning, oiling motors, changing filters, cleaning equipment, changing belts, changing oil and repairing equipment.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Assess and replace fan coil filters as required, make recommendations for large filter bank replacement.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Plus More: &lt;/strong&gt;Be ready to take on additional related tasks as assigned – your role is dynamic and essential to our success!&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;At the University of Regina, we’re more than just a campus – we’re a community!&lt;br&gt;Join our team and enjoy:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Meaningful Impact: &lt;/strong&gt;Your work directly contributes to creating a better environment for students, faculty, and staff.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Professional Growth: &lt;/strong&gt;We support your development, offering opportunities for advancement and learning.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work-Life Balance:&lt;/strong&gt; We value your well-being and know your personal life is most important!&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamic and Inclusive Workplace: &lt;/strong&gt;We value diversity and inclusivity. You’ll be part of a team that celebrates different perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences, making every day an opportunity for personal growth.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovation Culture: &lt;/strong&gt;We encourage fresh ideas and innovative thinking.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Competitive Compensation:&lt;/strong&gt; We offer competitive compensation package and benefits to reward your talent. A few of the these benefits include Health/Dental/Vision Benefits, flexible spending account, Defined Benefit Pension Plan, and much more!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div&gt;Join our Facilities Management team at the University of Regina and become a vital part of our mission to maintain a safe, efficient, and sustainable environment for our campus community.&lt;/div&gt;</content>\n    <author>\n      <name>Facilities Mgt - Operations Heating Plant Support</name>\n    </author>\n  </entry>\n</feed>"
    },
    "https://urcareers.uregina.ca/postings/search.atom?utf8=%E2%9C%93&query=&query_v0_posted_at_date=&435=&225=&1245%5B%5D=2&commit=Search": {
      "title": "",
      "description": "<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<feed xml:lang=\"en-US\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom\" xmlns:pa=\"urcareers.uregina.ca\">\n  <id>tag:urcareers.uregina.ca,2005:/postings/search</id>\n  <link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"text/html\" href=\"https://urcareers.uregina.ca\"/>\n  <link rel=\"self\" type=\"application/atom+xml\" href=\"https://urcareers.uregina.ca/postings/search.atom?utf8=%E2%9C%93&amp;query=&amp;query_v0_posted_at_date=&amp;435=&amp;225=&amp;1245%5B%5D=2&amp;commit=Search\"/>\n  <title>University of Regina: All Jobs</title>\n  <updated>2026-09-01T12:01:24-06:00</updated>\n  <entry>\n    <id>https://urcareers.uregina.ca/postings/22967</id>\n    <published>2026-09-01T12:01:24-06:00</published>\n    <updated>2026-09-01T12:01:24-06:00</updated>\n    <link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"text/html\" href=\"https://urcareers.uregina.ca/postings/22967\"/>\n    <title>Lab Instructor in Visual Communication Design, Media Design (One-Year Term)</title>\n    <content>&lt;div&gt;The Department of Creative Technologies and Design in the Faculty of Media, Art, and Performance (MAP) at the University of Regina invites highly qualified applicants for a one-year term Lab Instructor in Visual Communication Design and/or Media Design. This is a one-year term, with the possibility of renewal, to commence January 1, 2027, or July 1, 2027.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Joining an interdisciplinary team in Creative Technologies and Design, Fine Arts, Media, Computer Science, and Engineering, the successful candidate will bring technical expertise and critical thinking in the areas of Visual Communication Design and/or Media Design to build upon the well-established strengths of the Department of Creative Technologies and Design as we continue to expand our programs.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Teaching will include studio, lab-based, and lecture formats, as well as online and mixed modalities at the undergraduate level in Creative Technologies and Design. Previous studio/lab-based teaching experience at the University level in one or more of the areas of Visual Communication Design and Media Design, including Graphic Design, Web Design, Data Visualization, Advertising and Marketing Design, UI and UX Design, or Digital Interaction Design is required.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;The successful candidate will be expected to teach 7 undergraduate courses and contribute to service in the Department of Creative Technologies and Design and MAP.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;We acknowledge that within higher education in Canada, traditional or conventional academic and artistic pathways can reinforce biases in the filling of faculty and instructor positions. We encourage applications from those who may not fit all the qualifications and that challenge our ideas of teaching and artistic practice. We are particularly interested in colleagues who bring experience in facilitating equity, diversity and inclusion practices within their teaching, which may include contexts outside of the academic domain, including artistic praxis and community-based work.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Creative Technologies and Design seeks to attract candidates who identify with under-represented groups, and who are able to articulate a teaching philosophy that aligns with our values and complements and builds upon the established socially-engaged practices for which the Department is known. We seek a candidate whose expertise will enhance the University of Regina’s growing reputation as an important centre for a variety of teaching and research endeavours, including Indigenous art practices, disability/atypical creative practices, community wellness, social justice, community engaged creative practices, media arts, curation, exhibition and/or performance practices.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;The University of Regina is located in the heart of a vibrant, and increasingly diverse, mid-sized city in the center of the beautiful Canadian prairies on Treaty 4 Territory. The University has a student population of 16,000+ and is home to 10 faculties, including a multitude of academic departments and program areas. These units have established national and international reputations for excellence and innovative programs leading to bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degrees. The University has three federated colleges: First Nations University of Canada, Campion College, and Luther College. Our colleges bring further excellence and diversity to the educational experiences we offer.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;With a faculty complement of 35 full-time professors, including some of the most celebrated contemporary artists in the country, MAP enjoys a long-standing reputation as one of Western Canada’s foremost environments for scholarship and artistic research at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Emphasizing the importance of studio production and theory, we offer BA, BFA, BMus, MMus, MA, MFA, and an Interdisciplinary Studies PhD in Media and Artistic Practices.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;MAP works with other units, such as First Nations University of Canada, Women and Gender Studies, Social Work, Computer Science, Engineering, Business, Arts, Education, Kinesiology, and the Humanities Research Institute. MAP is home to the Centre for Socially Engaged Theatre (CSET), IMP Lab (Interactive Media and Performance), the VOICE Lab (Vocally Oriented Investigations in Creative Expression), RISC (Regina Improvisation Studies Centre). We have strong collaborative relationships with arts institutions, such as the MacKenzie Art Gallery, Regina Symphony Orchestra, Sâkêwêwak Artist Collective, Dunlop Art Gallery, Art Gallery of Regina, Regina Public Library, Neutral Ground, New Dance Horizons, Saskatchewan Film Pool, and Common Weal, among others. MAP has numerous international partnership universities, with many innovative mobility initiatives for both faculty and students in Mexico City and the UK, among other locations. MAP is now home to a new Canada Research Chair in Socially Engaged Theatre (Tier II) and the SaskPower Chair in Cultural Heritage.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;The University of Regina is strongly committed to employment equity within its communities and to recruiting a diverse faculty and staff.&lt;/div&gt;</content>\n    <author>\n      <name>Media, Art, and Performance-Other</name>\n    </author>\n  </entry>\n  <entry>\n    <id>https://urcareers.uregina.ca/postings/22779</id>\n    <published>2026-08-04T13:12:00-06:00</published>\n    <updated>2026-08-04T13:12:01-06:00</updated>\n    <link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"text/html\" href=\"https://urcareers.uregina.ca/postings/22779\"/>\n    <title>Tenure-Track Assistant Professor: Language and Literacy/Early Childhood Education</title>\n    <content>&lt;div&gt;The Faculty of Education at the University of Regina invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track&lt;strong&gt; Assistant Professor position in Language and Literacy/Early Childhood Education&lt;/strong&gt;, with an anticipated start date of&lt;strong&gt; January 1, 2027, or as negotiated with the successful candidate.&lt;/strong&gt; This hybrid position has a primary focus on early and emergent literacy with a connection to early childhood education.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;The University of Regina is located on Treaty 4 territory, with a presence in Treaty 6. These lands are home to the nêhiyawak, Anihšināpēk, Dakota, Lakota, and Nakoda peoples, and the homeland of the Métis/Michif Nation. With a population of over 270,000, Regina offers a rich blend of cultural, recreational, and entertainment opportunities—providing big-city amenities with a small-town feel.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;The Faculty of Education offers a variety of programs at both the undergraduate and graduate levels and engages in local, national, and international programs and projects in French and English. The Faculty of Education is committed to enacting social and ecological justice, indigenization, sustainability, cultural and linguistic diversity, life-long learning, service, outreach, and the collaborative processes that flourish in a community of caring and mutual respect. Our mission embodies commitments to community engagement, innovative research, and student success, as articulated in the University of Regina’s Strategic Plan &lt;em&gt;Together, We Serve: Community, Discovery, Impact.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Duties&lt;/strong&gt;: The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Language and Literacy, as well as selected Early Childhood Education courses. Expertise in reading pedagogies for young readers and emergent literacy development is required. The candidate will be expected to maintain an active program of scholarly research, independently and/or collaboratively, and to supervise and mentor graduate students. In addition, the successful candidate will contribute to collegial governance through service on faculty and university committees, as well as engagement with professional and broader communities.&lt;/div&gt;</content>\n    <author>\n      <name>Education-Dean's Office</name>\n    </author>\n  </entry>\n  <entry>\n    <id>https://urcareers.uregina.ca/postings/18787</id>\n    <published>2025-04-04T15:59:11-06:00</published>\n    <updated>2025-04-04T15:59:12-06:00</updated>\n    <link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"text/html\" href=\"https://urcareers.uregina.ca/postings/18787\"/>\n    <title>Assistant Professor, Developmental Psychology</title>\n    <content>&lt;div&gt;The Department of Psychology at the University of Regina is seeking applications for a full-time, tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor, with expertise in developmental psychology. The anticipated date of commencement is July 1, 2025, depending on the availability of the successful candidate.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Duties of the successful candidate will include teaching at the undergraduate and graduate level, honours and graduate thesis supervision, participation in departmental activities, and administrative service within the department. The successful candidate is expected to develop an independent program of research in developmental psychology that would be eligible for Tri-Council and/or Canada Foundation for Innovation funding.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;The University of Regina's Strategic Plan 2020-2025 (kahkiyaw kiwâhkômâkaninawak – All Our Relations) emphasizes Well-being and Belonging as a strategic priority, which includes prioritizing and supporting research in mental health. The Department of Psychology has been recognized as &lt;a href=\"https://www.timeshighereducation.com/world-university-rankings/2025/subject-ranking/psychology#!/length/25/sort_by/scores_citations/sort_order/asc/cols/scores\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;#1 in Canada and #2 in the world&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; in research quality, and is frequently &lt;a href=\"https://www.timeshighereducation.com/world-university-rankings/2022/subject-ranking/psychology#!/length/25/locations/CAN/sort_by/rank/sort_order/asc/cols/stats\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ranked among the top psychology departments in Canada&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. The Department offers two graduate programs, including the Experimental and Applied Psychology Graduate Program and the Clinical Psychology Graduate Program. The latter is accredited by the Canadian Psychological Association and has an on-site state-of-the-art Psychology Training Clinic. The Department maintains good relations with a number of health care, policing, research, and other educational facilities both within Regina and throughout the province.&lt;/div&gt;</content>\n    <author>\n      <name>Arts-Psychology</name>\n    </author>\n  </entry>\n  <entry>\n    <id>https://urcareers.uregina.ca/postings/17692</id>\n    <published>2024-11-25T11:24:21-06:00</published>\n    <updated>2024-11-25T11:24:21-06:00</updated>\n    <link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"text/html\" href=\"https://urcareers.uregina.ca/postings/17692\"/>\n    <title>Open-Rank Faculty Professor Position in Clinical Psychology</title>\n    <content>&lt;div&gt;The University of Regina is a vibrant and growing campus in a province with a booming economy. The Department of Psychology comprises a large undergraduate and honours program in addition to experimental and clinical graduate programs and has received numerous accolades for its research output and impact. Most recently, a paper published in Canadian Psychology (&lt;a href=\"https://dx.doi.org/10.1037/cap0000378\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;https://dx.doi.org/10.1037/cap0000378&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;) identified 3 department faculty as being amongst the top 15% most productive clinical psychologists in Canada.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;As part of an ongoing expansion of the Clinical Psychology Graduate Program, the Department of Psychology at the University of Regina is seeking applications for an open rank position in Clinical Psychology. Area of clinical research specialization is open, and rank of the position will be commensurate with experience. Date of commencement is negotiable depending on the availability of the successful candidate, but we wish to fill this position as soon as possible.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Duties of the successful candidate will include teaching at the undergraduate and graduate level, honours and graduate thesis supervision, supervision of clinical practicums, and participation in departmental activities. The successful candidate is expected to have an independent and active program of research in clinical psychology that would be eligible for Tri-Council and/or Canada Foundation for Innovation funding.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;The University of Regina's Strategic Plan 2020-2025 (kahkiyaw kiwâhkômâkaninawak – All Our Relations) emphasizes Well-being and Belonging as a strategic priority, which includes prioritizing and supporting research in mental health. The Clinical Psychology Graduate Program at the University of Regina is committed to the &lt;em&gt;scientist-practitioner&lt;/em&gt; model and is &lt;strong&gt;accredited by the Canadian Psychological Association&lt;/strong&gt;. The Clinical Psychology Graduate Program has an on-site state-of-the-art Psychology Training Clinic. The Department maintains good relations with a number of health care, research, and other educational facilities both within Regina and throughout the province.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Review of applications will continue until the position is filled.&lt;/div&gt;</content>\n    <author>\n      <name>Arts-Psychology</name>\n    </author>\n  </entry>\n</feed>"
    },
