    "https://urcareers.uregina.ca/postings/22779": {
      "title": "University of Regina Portal | Tenure-Track Assistant Professor: Language and Literacy/Early Childhood Education",
      "description": "University of Regina Portal | Tenure-Track Assistant Professor: Language and Literacy/Early Childhood Education Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help FAQs If you need assistance, please contact Human Resources at UofR.Recruitment@uregina.ca. Tenure-Track Assistant Professor: Language and Literacy/Early Childhood Education Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications must be submitted online at https://urcareers.uregina.... and should include: A cover letter that outlines your qualifications, teaching, and research interests A current curriculum vitae Names and contact information of three references A description of your scholarly research program A statement of your teaching philosophy Unofficial transcripts Candidates who are short-listed will be required to have three letters of reference and provide original transcripts addressed and sent to the Office of the Dean, Faculty of Education, University of Regina, 3737 Wascana Parkway, Regina, SK, S4S 0A2. For academic inquiries, please contact Dr. Jenn de Lugt, Associate Dean, Faculty Development & Human Resources, Faculty of Education ( Education.AssocDeanFDHR@uregina.ca ). Position Details Posting Summary Competition Number 20260133A/S Position Title Tenure-Track Assistant Professor: Language and Literacy/Early Childhood Education Faculty/Department Faculty of Education Unit Education-Dean's Office Employee Group URFA Collective Agreement Consideration Open to the Public. CUPE 5791 Job Family N/A Category Academic Number of Vacancies 1 Position Summary The Faculty of Education at the University of Regina invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Language and Literacy/Early Childhood Education , with an anticipated start date of January 1, 2027, or as negotiated with the successful candidate. This hybrid position has a primary focus on early and emergent literacy with a connection to early childhood education. The University of Regina is located on Treaty 4 territory, with a presence in Treaty 6. These lands are home to the nêhiyawak, Anihšināpēk, Dakota, Lakota, and Nakoda peoples, and the homeland of the Métis/Michif Nation. With a population of over 270,000, Regina offers a rich blend of cultural, recreational, and entertainment opportunities—providing big-city amenities with a small-town feel. The Faculty of Education offers a variety of programs at both the undergraduate and graduate levels and engages in local, national, and international programs and projects in French and English. The Faculty of Education is committed to enacting social and ecological justice, indigenization, sustainability, cultural and linguistic diversity, life-long learning, service, outreach, and the collaborative processes that flourish in a community of caring and mutual respect. Our mission embodies commitments to community engagement, innovative research, and student success, as articulated in the University of Regina’s Strategic Plan Together, We Serve: Community, Discovery, Impact. Duties : The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Language and Literacy, as well as selected Early Childhood Education courses. Expertise in reading pedagogies for young readers and emergent literacy development is required. The candidate will be expected to maintain an active program of scholarly research, independently and/or collaboratively, and to supervise and mentor graduate students. In addition, the successful candidate will contribute to collegial governance through service on faculty and university committees, as well as engagement with professional and broader communities. Position Requirements The required qualifications for this position include a Ph.D. degree or the near completion of a Ph.D. ( ABD ) in a relevant area, as well as teaching and research experience related to: reading acquisition, reading assessment, writing and multimodal pedagogies, multilingual learners or contexts, early and elementary-level literacies, and/or emergent literacies. The successful candidate will have a clearly articulated and active program of research or scholarship related to early literacy and reading pedagogies in the early elementary years. Experience teaching reading and literacy in K-3 contexts is preferred. Teaching experience in university settings is considered an asset. Expertise in one or more areas of early childhood education is also considered an asset, including early years curriculum and assessment, play-based pedagogy, child development, and anti-oppressive education in early learning settings. Physical Demands Pay Grade Faculty Assistant Professor Salary Range $101,603 - $128,323 as per the URFA Collective Agreement. Status Permanent Work Hours Duration (if Term/Temporary) Full-Time/Part-Time Full Time Preference Posting No Preference Target Posting Not Targeted Additional Information Contact Information For academic inquiries, please contact Dr. Jenn de Lugt, Associate Dean, Faculty Development & Human Resources, Faculty of Education (Education.AssocDeanFDHR@uregina.ca) Job Open Date 08/01/2026 Job Close Date 09/30/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Application Instructions Applications must be submitted online at https://urcareers.uregina…. and should include: A cover letter that outlines your qualifications, teaching, and research interests A current curriculum vitae Names and contact information of three references A description of your scholarly research program A statement of your teaching philosophy Unofficial transcripts Candidates who are short-listed will be required to have three letters of reference and provide original transcripts addressed and sent to the Office of the Dean, Faculty of Education, University of Regina, 3737 Wascana Parkway, Regina, SK, S4S 0A2. For academic inquiries, please contact Dr. Jenn de Lugt, Associate Dean, Faculty Development & Human Resources, Faculty of Education ( Education.AssocDeanFDHR@uregina.ca ). Safety Statement The University is committed to maintaining a safe and healthy workplace and strengthening a culture of safety across the campus community. All employees share responsibility for contributing to a safe working environment. Diversity Statement The University of Regina is committed to an inclusive workplace that reflects the richness of the community that we serve. The University welcomes applications from all qualified individuals, including individuals within the University’s employment equity categories of women, persons with disabilities, members of visible minorities, Indigenous persons, individuals of diverse gender and sexual orientation and all groups protected by The Saskatchewan Human Rights Code, 2018. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Required Required Documents Cover Letter Resume/Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Reference Contact Info Research Interests/Projects Unofficial Transcript(s) Optional Documents If you need assistance, please contact Human Resources at UofR.Recruitment@uregina.ca . To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
